#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "02ae40ba-a02c-5025-9597-1968322f2421" :question/math-academy-id "e-2279" :question/problem "In a ballet school, the ratio of the number of students with black hair to the total number of students is $5: 8$. If there are $25$ students with black hair, how many students are there in ballet school who don't have black hair?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}8}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}}{{\\color{red}8}}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students with black hair and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe know that there are $25$ students with black hair, so we want to make a numerator of $25$. We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}\\times 5}{{\\color{red}8}\\times 5} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}25}}{{\\color{red}40}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since there are $25$ students with black hair, there must be $40$ students at the ballet school. Of this amount, the number of students who do not have black hair is\n\n$$\n40 - 25 = 15\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "4aeb615e-16a1-5170-be5e-fe0f63a5d895" :question/math-academy-id "e-2280" :question/problem "In a Chicago hospital, the ratio of the number of boys born to the total number of babies born is $\\dfrac{4}{9}$. If $100$ boys were born in that hospital in a particular month, how many girls were born that month?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of the number of boys born to the total number of babies born is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{9}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of boys born and the denominator represents the total number of babies born.\n\nWe know that $100$ boys were born, so we want to make a numerator of $100$. We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $25$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}4}\\times 25}{{\\color{red}9}\\times 25} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}100}}{{\\color{red}225}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $100$ boys were born, $225$ babies were born during that month. Of this amount, the number of girls was\n\n$$\n225 - 100 = 125\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191d936f-100a-528b-b3c8-96bc92975a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252867} {:answer/id #uuid "a571e587-f301-503e-8ce8-c664df5399ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252868} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fec51c-bfce-5c10-af85-2e45d402a860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252869} {:answer/id #uuid "a14cea27-41ed-569d-9a66-15a0a46b8e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252870} {:answer/id #uuid "3d373b37-3d55-53d6-b5f3-db76b882f3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9fec51c-bfce-5c10-af85-2e45d402a860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252869} :answer-field/id #uuid "031f89e7-6550-5618-8c6f-17718cd5a9b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252866}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "981cb151-225b-5f7f-9223-5435f3713133" :question/math-academy-id "q-147065" :question/problem "The ratio of yellow to white tulips in Mia's flower garden is $5:4.$\nIf Mia has $30$ yellow tulips, how many tulips are in the flower garden?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $5:4$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of yellow tulips, and the denominator represents the number of white tulips.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 6}{4\\times 6}=\\frac{30}{24}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  Mia has $30$ yellow and $24$ white tulips. So, the total number of tulips is \n\n$$\n30+24=54.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dacc8fe-e1d3-56ef-9658-a0f0d744fd33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252874} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e6d0d2-db10-54e1-9d25-513a56951f82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252875} {:answer/id #uuid "91b22ed9-f39e-5ff0-8a05-9a0915585b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252876} {:answer/id #uuid "c5b2c101-a0e5-501b-8cad-6f51fa2176de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252877} {:answer/id #uuid "09edee87-aaf2-516e-8730-78934f0c2762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91b22ed9-f39e-5ff0-8a05-9a0915585b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252876} :answer-field/id #uuid "590cf8b1-83ec-501d-b6af-13ff123b704f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18131c5f-3ae2-5978-9dc3-079e0144c30f" :question/math-academy-id "q-147069" :question/problem "A die was rolled $40$ times, landing on an odd number in $\\frac{5}{8}$ of the rolls. How many times did it come up with an even number?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of rolls in which the die landed on an odd number to the total number of rolls is $\\frac{5}{8}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of rolls resulting in an odd number, and the denominator represents the total number of rolls.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $40$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 5}{8\\times 5}=\\frac{25}{40}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the die landed on an odd number $25$ times.\nSo, the number of times the die landed on an even number is\n\n$$\n40-25=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0a6cff7-aaf4-5d71-a41c-4820cf60c15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252881} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5136c1-677f-59a8-be3c-2f7ca7140b9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252882} {:answer/id #uuid "2d17cb40-4698-5763-8234-245ecdf7d7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252883} {:answer/id #uuid "201ce330-bfed-5c99-9af0-fc991066b16f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252884} {:answer/id #uuid "fa43f59a-a54b-5117-9f35-3f6c624157da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201ce330-bfed-5c99-9af0-fc991066b16f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252884} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6cbbf9-10ea-52fb-b510-d9a7e0c6e6e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35f611e8-e212-5bce-bd69-8146cf7fb84d" :question/math-academy-id "q-147075" :question/problem "Jack writes down a number with multiple digits.\nThe ratio of even digits in the number to the total number of digits is $1:3.$\nIf the number has $7$ even digits, how many odd digits are there?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $1:3$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of even digits, and the denominator represents the total number of digits.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $7$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 7}{3\\times 7}=\\frac{7}{21}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $21$ digits in total. \nSo, the number of odd digits in the number is\n\n$$\n21-7=14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ee90e89-5bb1-521f-a59f-f075f4d1223e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252888} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3550e7-c5d5-5fd7-b756-780746a7d59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252889} {:answer/id #uuid "02e23d35-0f7c-5634-b655-ed36c91321ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252890} {:answer/id #uuid "e21344c4-831f-5bac-a3ae-621075c14d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252891} {:answer/id #uuid "a462d389-968a-5051-95a0-99adc6016464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ee90e89-5bb1-521f-a59f-f075f4d1223e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252888} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c81c5ca-072c-5e32-b475-c9a712b74568" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252887}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8fcba180-254a-510d-b667-40abfdc30f60" :question/math-academy-id "q-147076" :question/problem "In a table, each cell was colored either yellow or green. The ratio of yellow cells to the total number of cells is $2:3.$ If there are $24$ yellow cells, how many cells were colored green?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of yellow cells to the total number of cells is $\\frac{2}{3}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of yellow cells, and the denominator represents the total number of cells.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $24$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 12}{3\\times 12}=\\frac{24}{36}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $36$ cells in the table. \nSo, the number of green cells is\n\n$$\n36-24=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279c6889-0537-5226-a204-0fb0ea75b77b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252895} {:answer/id #uuid "28bdae41-6923-5282-bc49-fe3a00abd025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252896} {:answer/id #uuid "7bbdc896-c607-5aaf-ba3b-b0fa1594d673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252897} {:answer/id #uuid "61932a42-0dd0-5993-a40a-c0e0de6be2a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252898} {:answer/id #uuid "f605f4fc-74ae-51ee-8d76-1b2ed821569b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28bdae41-6923-5282-bc49-fe3a00abd025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252896} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d2d883-240a-5f1c-91ea-2bc381bfdec8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252894}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9477d3a-e0b3-5de2-b961-481217c4236a" :question/math-academy-id "q-147213" :question/problem "A bag contains blue and green buttons. The ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $2:7.$ If there are $14$ blue buttons,  how many green buttons are in the bag?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $\\frac{2}{7}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of blue buttons, and the denominator represents the total number of buttons.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $14$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 7}{7\\times 7}=\\frac{14}{49}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $49$ buttons in the bag. \nSo, the number of green buttons is\n\n$$\n49-14=35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ccf9fe1-2ca0-571a-9a19-c77299cbba51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178878} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fb44c8-a0ff-5966-90d1-ea1618435057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178879} {:answer/id #uuid "1242c19a-8fad-5620-840c-9f5d85b71c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178880} {:answer/id #uuid "350fcdd3-08e5-573a-8461-e9b2566545fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178881} {:answer/id #uuid "49665566-fa96-5af9-bd23-8304722f65e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49665566-fa96-5af9-bd23-8304722f65e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178882} :answer-field/id #uuid "28469468-6fc2-52c5-a538-523e17d18e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178877}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6604770-26c5-5386-84c1-792391047167" :question/math-academy-id "q-59887" :question/problem "The ratio of girls to boys in a chess club is $2: 1$. If there are $10$ girls, then how many members does the club have in total?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $2:1$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of girls, and the denominator represents the number of boys.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $10$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{10}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $10$ girls and $5$ boys in the club. So the total number of members is \n\n$$\n10+5=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c59ba6f6-4740-5694-b646-ac3053792599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178884} {:answer/id #uuid "463173dc-1b01-5650-90c7-3526db97079b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178885} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2ac047-4457-569a-8e43-99c4c816eb41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178886} {:answer/id #uuid "79ca2378-b680-5c59-a7fb-a43eb8b90846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178887} {:answer/id #uuid "79ffc13e-ffed-5ac2-be33-5b07eba9c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ffc13e-ffed-5ac2-be33-5b07eba9c5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178888} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a46319f-5e83-5ed8-82b0-8a27a0343225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178883}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9aff327a-3ab5-5bdb-b2ab-437fac7b7394" :question/math-academy-id "q-59895" :question/problem "There are $15$ students in a class, and $\\frac{2}{5}$ of them wear glasses. How many students do not wear glasses?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of students who wear glasses to the total number of students is $\\frac{2}{5}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students who wear glasses, and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 3}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{6}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $6$ students who wear glasses. \n\nSo the number of students who don't wear glasses is\n\n$$\n15-6=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e1f2ed-4b99-5b9a-a918-d73172636b7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252902} {:answer/id #uuid "193f33da-d526-5993-9fe9-e23464e059c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252903} {:answer/id #uuid "97b61f14-3872-523d-9ba2-0c30474e8dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252904} {:answer/id #uuid "ba8a9a24-45ca-59cf-b597-39151a7111ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252905} {:answer/id #uuid "0d079b28-a9ad-5ccf-a0f0-87b0e136d217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "193f33da-d526-5993-9fe9-e23464e059c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252903} :answer-field/id #uuid "e382c57a-9214-56dc-9f6d-4e997c975621" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252901}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24c0c9bf-efcd-5479-9d82-7464c16f2610" :question/math-academy-id "q-60139" :question/problem "One day, $20$ adults and some children attended a music festival at Beethoven Park. If the ratio of adults to children was $4:7$, how many people attended the park that day?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $4:7$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of adults and the denominator represents the number of children.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 5}{7\\times 5}=\\frac{20}{35}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20$ adults and $35$ children attended that day. Thus, the total number of people who went to the park that day was\n\n$$\n20+35=55.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252907 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "884cd7c2-01af-5434-954c-2bad2b76fd53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252909} {:answer/id #uuid "598f4e4f-addd-5654-83a4-e0da0b36e120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252910} {:answer/id #uuid "ba8f9c3a-fb08-5c32-b5c3-461298bbd5b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252911} {:answer/id #uuid "d15608ed-4657-54a9-b88a-23f38f7017f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252912} {:answer/id #uuid "bc958ee0-eaf7-529c-b22c-263f4b0bf0b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc958ee0-eaf7-529c-b22c-263f4b0bf0b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252913} :answer-field/id #uuid "9df75cf1-7961-5a6f-8293-eac424a86e58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252908}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2ac6a51-e2c1-5822-97ee-00799ffc99ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-60185" :question/problem "Jason has apples and peaches in his kitchen. The ratio of the number of apples to the total number of fruits Jason has is $6:7.$ If Jason has $30$ apples, how many peaches does he have?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $6:7$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{7}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of apples and the denominator represents the total number of fruits.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 5}{7\\times 5}=\\frac{30}{35}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Jason has $35$ fruits in total. So, the number of peaches Jason has is\n\n$$\n35-30=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e78f491f-2ad0-5eee-bb48-5b935943fe89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252916} {:answer/id #uuid "f641e7e3-d77c-5301-8fc7-f0c6084b5dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252917} {:answer/id #uuid "1e65cf1c-94ae-5599-95b1-860a443bcaf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252918} {:answer/id #uuid "dc72e729-7f85-51f7-a701-27baa463e02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252919} {:answer/id #uuid "fed6c063-411e-5e42-b59d-ae00306b0dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f641e7e3-d77c-5301-8fc7-f0c6084b5dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252917} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3204333-0fc4-5209-8ad4-ad30354f3e1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252915}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23d6df1d-9c8b-5bf7-91a5-28904190b917" :question/math-academy-id "q-92849" :question/problem "A rock band has $48$ songs, $\\frac{1}{4}$ of which are ballads. How many of the band's songs are not ballads?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of ballads to the total number of songs is $\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of ballads, and the denominator represents the total number of songs .\n\nWe can make a denominator of $48$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 12}{4\\times 12}=\\frac{12}{48}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the band has $12$ ballads. \n\nSo the number of songs that are not ballads is\n\n$$\n48-12=36.\n$$"}]}
